        "decoDesc": {
            "id": -5875889708796213005,
            "text": "This is really odd. Originium formations are usually stable and would neither metastasize nor grow. But the Originium near the Originium Gorge exhibited signs of slow and steady growth despite normal ambient conditions. \nI don't know what's affecting it. \nWe've established a surveillance camp and triangulated the source via our nearby mining sites. All readings point to something within the Originium Gorge. But the Originium formations inside the place are just too thick. It was impossible for us to head in for detailed surveillance. \nPerhaps we can use our prospecting machines. Upgrading them might give us a solution."
